in the beginning when i opened my first  store in venice i had no money at that  point so i literally put my personal  stuff on the walls my personal record  collection my personal skateboards and i  painted everything myself because i had  no budget for that so i don't know it's  just this whole kind of part of the  brand and my passion and the lifestyle  that i think you know leaves people  feeling good  i'm paige maikoski i'm the founder and  president of aviator nation  aviator nation is a lifestyle brand that  ultimately was created to bring people  together and  make quality clothing in america that  makes you feel comfortable and good  about yourself  fashion is honestly probably one of the  most competitive businesses out there i  think for me the made in america thing  is a huge part of that because  most companies even the companies that  start out with made in america end up  taking it overseas and now that i've  done this for 16 years and i'm still  making it in california where it's very  expensive obviously to make clothes you  know i think that that makes me feel  like i'm doing something different and  better  than a lot of other companies  i was actually living in california and  i was working in a surf shop and i was  doing photography freelance i thought  photography was my path but it was when  i was working in the surf shop and i was  around  clothing all the time that i realized i  had such a crazy passion  for the clothing and i would look at  clothes and be like i like that but i  want it to be this color i wanted to  have a different design and i just  became kind of obsessed with it and so i  bought a sewing machine and just started  making clothes for myself and i would  stay up late at night after work and  literally sew for hours trying to get  the fit right and the design right  and it wasn't just a fun little hobby it  was truly a passion and i became kind of  obsessed with it  once i had it to where i thought it was  perfect then i started  selling it at a street festival and so  that first time that i sold it at the  festival i think i paid like 500 for the  booth and i ended up making 8 000  in one day at a street fair so  pretty much immediately i was like i  need to quit my job at the surf shop and  just focus on this if i can make eight  thousand dollars in one day  there's a business here  fred seagull was the store in santa  monica that really took a chance on new  designers and so one day i rolled in  like my rack of clothes that i had  literally sewn in my garage and the the  buyer was blown away she was like i love  this it's amazing she bought everything  and she placed an order for close to  nine grand then literally one weekend  went by she called me on monday morning  and she said paige everything sold out  we need more we need to figure this out  like we need regular deliveries i  immediately went downtown and i went  door-to-door in factories starting to  look for sewers and build my team  in the beginning having no experience  and no formal training and just kind of  doing it the way that i  made sense to me drawing it by hand you  know ended up going into the early  designs and people loved that about the  clothes they loved that it was a little  bit imperfect you know and it wasn't  computer generated graphics which is  pretty much what most people do my thing  was i really wanted the clothes to look  vintage the machines that we use for  screen printing are different than what  most people use so we don't use all the  fancy new techniques most companies  would send garments through a basic wash  process that you know takes like 20  minutes or something like that i mean  our stuff is in the wash for like an  hour and a half and that's what i'm  passionate about because i want it to  feel vintage when you're buying it  [Music]  when i decided to start opening more  stores i wanted to make sure that the  store was really you know it had posters  and memorabilia and stuff from the  actual community so for example we're  here on the austin store there's a lot  of albums of artists that are from here  there's posters of willie nelson and  jason confused these are like iconic  figures that came from texas it  definitely makes each store super unique  and special to the community that it's  in  watching other companies and watching  the quality kind of go backwards i think  i always you know told myself i never  want that to happen i want our quality  to just get better there's corners you  can cut every day to make a lot more  money but if you're focused on the  quality like the customers are going to  stay and they're going to grow and  they're going to tell their friends and  that's what ultimately really makes us  successful  the reality is as an entrepreneur what  you start is about to become your entire  life so if you don't love it  this is going to suck for you you know  what i mean so like start with what you  love to do and then try to make that  your business because it's going to be  your life and then the money and all  that just comes because if you're doing  what you love people see that and they  want to be part of that the money will  come forget about the money  [Music]
 

